"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C001\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says Rule 6c-11 requires written basket policies and procedures covering basket construction and acceptance.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Mentions detailed custom-basket parameters and a process for revisions or deviations. It omits that the parameters must be in the best interests of the fund and its shareholders.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that the policies must specify the titles or roles of adviser employees who review each custom basket for compliance, and that review records must be kept.\"},{\"point\":4,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Defines a custom basket to include a non-representative basket and a representative basket that differs from the initial basket used that business day. It also says a non-standard order is not a Rule 6c-11 category and does not by itself make a basket custom.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":\"\\\"(2) a representative basket that is non-pro-rata or differs from that initial basket\\\". Under Rule 6c-11, a representative basket is custom only if it differs from the initial basket used that business day. Being non-pro-rata does not make it custom. This misstates the custom-basket definition, which is a material local falsehood that caps the grade at partial.\",\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"All four required points are substantively addressed, totalling 3.5 of 4. There is no central error: the answer does not limit custom baskets to non-standard orders and does not say a later differing representative basket can never be custom. However, it wrongly says a non-pro-rata representative basket is a custom basket, a material local falsehood. Under the scoring rule this caps the grade at partial.\"}","ttft_ms":9146,"type":"result","duration_ms":13556,"uuid":"fcd6a281-3512-4bc4-ae2f-9e70120502fd","ttft_stream_ms":1128,"time_to_request_ms":77,"first_content_frame_ms":1128,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
